#. Tag: title
#: chap.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>PAP</acronym> and <acronym>CHAP</acronym>"
msgstr "<acronym>PAP</acronym> i <acronym>CHAP</acronym>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Starting with version 0.9.1, &kppp; has supported directly the most commonly "
"used form of <acronym>PAP</acronym> authentication."
msgstr ""
"Počevši od verzije 0.9.1, &kppp; podržava direktno najčešće korišteni oblik "
"<acronym>PAP</acronym> ovjere."

#. Tag: title
#: chap.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>PAP</acronym> with &kppp;"
msgstr "<acronym>PAP</acronym> sa &kppp;"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two different ways to use <acronym>PAP</acronym>."
msgstr "Postoje dva različita načina korištenja <acronym>PAP</acronym>."

#. Tag: title
#: chap.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "Client side authentication"
msgstr "Ovjera sa strane klijenta"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This variant is used by many commercial <acronym>ISP</acronym>'s. It "
"basically means that you (or rather, your computer) must authenticate "
"yourself to the <acronym>ISP</acronym>'s <acronym>PPP</acronym> server. The "
"<acronym>PPP</acronym> server does not need to authenticate itself to your "
"computer. This is no security issue, as you should know which computer you "
"just tried to dial to."
msgstr ""
"Ovu varijantu koriste mnogi komercijalni <acronym>ISP</acronym> 'vi. To u "
"osnovi znači da (ili bolje rečeno, vaš računar) morate potvrditi svoju "
"ovjeru na <acronym>ISP</acronym>'u<acronym>PPP</acronym> serveru. "
"<acronym>PPP</acronym> server ne treba da ovjeri sebe za vaš računar. Ovo "
"nije pitanje sigurnosti, zato što bi trebali znati koji računar ste upravo "
"pokušali da birate."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your <acronym>ISP</acronym> gives you a username and password, and tells "
"you to use <acronym>PAP</acronym> authentication, this is the variant you "
"should choose."
msgstr ""
"Ako vaš <acronym>ISP</acronym> vam daje korisničko ime i lozinku, i kaže vam "
"da koristite <acronym>PAP</acronym> ovjeru, ovo je varijanta koju bi trebali "
"izabrati."

#. Tag: title
#: chap.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Two way authentication"
msgstr "Dvostruka ovjera"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As above, but in this case your computer requires the <acronym>ISP</acronym> "
"<acronym>PPP</acronym> server to authenticate itself. In order to establish "
"a connection, you must chose the authentication method <guilabel>Script "
"based</guilabel>, not <guilabel>PAP</guilabel>, and you will have to "
"manually edit <filename>/etc/ppp/pap-secrets</filename>. While &kppp; "
"doesn't provide built in support for this variant, it is nevertheless easy "
"to establish a connection."
msgstr ""
"Kao što je gore, ali u ovom slučaju vaš računar zahtijeva <acronym>ISP</"
"acronym> <acronym>PPP</acronym> server za svoju ovjeru. U cilju "
"uspostavljanja veze, morate odabrati metodu provjere autentičnosti "
"<guilabel>Skripta bazirano</guilabel>, a ne <guilabel>PAP</guilabel>, i vi "
"ćete morati da ručno uredite <filename>/etc/ppp/pap-secrets</filename>. Dok "
"&kppp; ne pruža ugrađenu podrškom za ovu varijantu, ipak je lahko "
"uspostaviti vezu."

#. Tag: title
#: chap.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "Preparing &kppp; for <acronym>PAP</acronym>"
msgstr "Pripremanje &kppp; za <acronym>PAP</acronym>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make sure that the file <filename>/etc/ppp/options</filename> (and "
"<filename>&tilde;/.ppprc</filename> if it exists) do <emphasis>not</"
"emphasis> contain one of the following arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Budite sigurni da datoteka <filename>/etc/ppp/options</filename> (i "
"<filename>&tilde;/.ppprc</filename> ako postoji) <emphasis>ne</emphasis> "
"sadrži jedan od sljedećih argumenata:"

#. Tag: option
#: chap.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "+pap"
msgstr "+pap"

#. Tag: option
#: chap.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "-pap"
msgstr "-pap"

#. Tag: option
#: chap.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "papcrypt"
msgstr "papcrypt"

#. Tag: option
#: chap.docbook:61 chap.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "+chap"
msgstr "+chap"

#. Tag: option
#: chap.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>+ua</option>"
msgstr "<option>+ua</option>"

#. Tag: option
#: chap.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "remotename"
msgstr "ime udaljenog"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is very unlikely that any of these options are already there, but just to "
"be sure, please check."
msgstr ""
"Vrlo je vjerovatno da je bilo koja od ovih opcija već tu, ali samo da bi "
"bili sigurni, molimo vas provjerite."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start &kppp;"
msgstr "Pokrenite &kppp;"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>Configure</guibutton>"
msgstr "Kliknite <guibutton>Konfiguriranje</guibutton>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the account you want to use <acronym>PAP</acronym> with and click "
"<guibutton>Edit</guibutton>"
msgstr ""
"Izaberite račun sa kojim želite koristiti <acronym>PAP</acronym> i kliknite "
"<guibutton>Uredi</guibutton>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose the <guilabel>Dial</guilabel> tab"
msgstr "Izaberite <guilabel>Biraj</guilabel> tabular"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <acronym>PAP</acronym> in the <guilabel>Authentication</guilabel> "
"drop down box."
msgstr ""
"Odaberite <acronym>PAP</acronym> u <guilabel>Ovjera</guilabel> padajućem "
"okviru."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want to retype the password each time you dial in, select "
"<guilabel>Store password</guilabel>. This will save the password to a file, "
"so make sure that nobody else has access to your account."
msgstr ""
"Ako ne želite da ponovo unosite lozinku svaki put kad birate, odaberite "
"<guilabel>Čuvaj lozinku</guilabel>. Ovo će spasiti lozinku u datoteku, zato "
"budite sigurni da niko drugi nema pristup vašem račun."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"That's it. Close the dialogs, type in the username and password your "
"<acronym>ISP</acronym> supplied, and click <guibutton>Connect</guibutton>."
msgstr ""
"To je to. Zatvorite dijaloge, ukucajte korisničko ime i lozinku u "
"<acronym>ISP</acronym>, i kliknite <guibutton>Spoji</guibutton>."

#. Tag: title
#: chap.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An alternative method of using <acronym>PAP</acronym> and <acronym>CHAP</"
"acronym> with &kppp;"
msgstr ""
"Alternativna metoda korištenja <acronym>PAP</acronym> i <acronym>CHAP</"
"acronym> sa &kppp;"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section is based on an email from Keith Brown <email>kbrown@pdq.net</"
"email> and explains how to make &kppp; work with a generic <acronym>PAP</"
"acronym> or <acronym>CHAP</acronym> account. If your <acronym>ISP</acronym> "
"just gave you a user id and a password for an account, you probably can skip "
"this section, and the instructions in the previous one will be all you need."
msgstr ""
"Ovaj odjeljak je zasnovan na mailu od Keith Browna <email>kbrown@pdq.net</"
"email> i objašnjava kako napraviti da &kppp; radi sa generičkim "
"<acronym>PAP</acronym> ili <acronym>CHAP</acronym> računom. Ako vaš "
"<acronym>ISP</acronym> vam upravo da korisnički id i lozinku za račun, "
"vjerovatno možete preskočiti ovaj odjeljak, a instrukcije u prethodnom su "
"sve što vam treba."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>PAP</acronym> seems a lot more complicated at first glance than it "
"really is. The server (the machine you are connecting to) basically tells "
"the client (your machine) to authenticate using <acronym>PAP</acronym>. The "
"client (<application>pppd</application>) looks in a specific file for an "
"entry that contains a matching server name, and a client name for this "
"connection, and then sends the password it finds there. That's about it!"
msgstr ""
"<acronym>PAP</acronym> izgleda mnogo složeniji nego što jeste na prvi "
"pogled. Server (mašina na koju se povezujete) u osnovi govori klijentu (vaš "
"uređaj) da provjeri autentičnost pomoću <acronym>PAP</acronym>. Klijent "
"(<application>pppd</application>) gleda u određenu datoteku za unos koja "
"sadrži ime podudarajućeg servera, i ime klijenta za ovo spajanje, a zatim "
"šalje lozinku koju nađe tamo. To je sve!"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now here's how to make that happen. I am assuming a <acronym>pppd</acronym> "
"version of 2.2.x or better and a standard installation of configuration "
"files under <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/ppp</filename>."
msgstr ""
"Evo kako to da se dogodi. Ja pretpostavljam <acronym>pppd</acronym> verziju "
"2.2.x ili veću i standardna instalacija konfiguracijske datoteke pod "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/etc/ppp</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For the purposes of illustration, imagine that you have an internet account "
"with <systemitem>glob.net</systemitem> with the username "
"<systemitem>userbaz</systemitem> and the password <literal>foobar</literal>"
msgstr ""
"Za potrebe ilustracije, zamislite da imate internet račun kod "
"<systemitem>glob.net</systemitem> s korisničkim imenom "
"<systemitem>korisnikbaz</systemitem> i lozinku <literal>foobar</literal>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, you need to add all this to a file called <filename>/etc/ppp/pap-"
"secrets</filename>. The format of an entry for our purposes is:"
msgstr ""
"Prvo, trebate dodati sve to u datoteku pod nazivom <filename>/etc/ppp/pap-"
"secrets</filename>. Format unosa za naše svrhe je:"

#. Tag: screen
#: chap.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>USERNAME    SERVERNAME     PASSWORD</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>KORISNIČKO IME  SERVERIME  LOZINKA</userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So you would add the following line to <filename>/etc/ppp/pap-secrets</"
"filename> and then save it :"
msgstr ""
"Dakle, vi dodajte sljedeću liniju na <filename>/etc/ppp/pap-secrets</"
"filename>, a zatim je sačuvajte:"

#. Tag: screen
#: chap.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>userbaz     glob           foobar</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>korisnikbaz glob foobar</userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use any name for the server you wish, so long as you use the same "
"name in the <application>pppd</application> arguments, as you'll see "
"shortly. Here it's been shortened to <userinput>glob</userinput>, but this "
"name is only used to locate the correct password."
msgstr ""
"Možete koristiti bilo koje ime za server koji želite, sve dok koristite isto "
"ime u <application>pppd</application> argumenti, kao što ćete vidjeti "
"uskoro. Ovdje je to skraćeno na <userinput>glob</userinput>, ali ovo ime se "
"koristi samo za lociranje ispravne lozinke."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next you need to set up the connection in &kppp;. The basics are the same as "
"any other connection, so we won't go into details here, except to say that "
"you probably want to make sure that <filename>/etc/ppp/options</filename> is "
"empty, and you don't want to create a login script either."
msgstr ""
"Sljedeće trebate podesiti spajanje u &kppp;. Osnove su iste kao i za bilo "
"koje drugo spajanje, tako da nećemo ići u detalje ovdje, osim što ćemo reći "
"da vjerovatno želite biti sigurni da je <filename>/etc/ppp/options</"
"filename> prazna, a vi također ne želite stvoriti skriptu za prijavljivanje."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the &kppp; settings dialog, at the bottom of the <guilabel>Dial</"
"guilabel> tab, is a <guibutton>Customize pppd Arguments</guibutton> button. "
"This brings up an editing dialog. Here you can enter values that will be "
"sent to <application>pppd</application> as command line arguments, and in "
"the case of multiple value arguments, you need to enter each value as a "
"separate entry in the listbox, in the correct order."
msgstr ""
"U &kppp; dijalogu postavki, na dnu <guilabel>Biraj</guilabel>, je "
"<guibutton>Prilagodi pppd</guibutton>. To dovodi do dijaloga uređivanja. "
"Ovdje možete unijeti vrijednosti koje će biti poslane na <application>pppd</"
"application> kao argumenti komandne linije, a u slučaju kada imamo više "
"vrijednosti argumenata, potrebno je da unesete svaku vrijednost kao poseban "
"unos u okvir listu, u ispravnom redoslijedu."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can put in any other arguments you want first. Then add the arguments "
"that <application>pppd</application> uses to handle <acronym>PAP</acronym> "
"authentication. In this example, we are going to add <userinput>user</"
"userinput>, <userinput>userbaz</userinput>, <userinput>remotename</"
"userinput> and <userinput>glob</userinput> in that order."
msgstr ""
"Možete staviti bilo koji drugi argument ako želite kao prvi. Zatim dodajte "
"argumente koje <application>pppd</application> koristi za rukovanje "
"<acronym>PAP</acronym> ovjerom. U ovom primjeru, mi ćemo dodati "
"<userinput>korisnik</userinput>, <userinput>korisnikbaz</userinput>, "
"<userinput>ime udaljenog</userinput> i <userinput>glob</userinput> u tom "
"redoslijedu."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <option>user</option> tells the <application>pppd</application> what "
"user name to look for in the <filename>pap-secrets</filename> file and then "
"to send to the server. The remotename is used by <application>pppd</"
"application> to match the entry in the <filename>pap-secrets</filename> "
"file, so again, it can be anything you want so long as it is consistent with "
"the entry in the <filename>pap-secrets</filename> file."
msgstr ""
"<option>korisnik</option> govori <application>pppd</application> koje "
"korisničko ime da traži u <filename>pap-secrets</filename> datoteci i zatim "
"šalje na server. Ime udaljenog se koristi od <application>pppd</application> "
"tako da odgovara ulazu u <filename>pap-secrets</filename> datoteku ali opet, "
"to može biti sve što želite sve dok je to u skladu sa ulazom u <filename>pap-"
"secrets</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#: chap.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"That's all there is to it, and you should now be able to set up your own "
"connection to a server with <acronym>PAP</acronym> authentication. "
"<acronym>CHAP</acronym> is not much different. You can see the &Linux; "
"Network Administrators Guide for a <filename>chap-secrets</filename> file "
"format, and the <application>pppd</application> arguments used, and the rest "
"should be simple."
msgstr ""
"To je sve što se ima reći, a ti bi sada trebao biti u mogućnosti da postaviš "
"svoj vlastiti priključak na server sa <acronym>PAP</acronym> ovjerom. "
"<acronym>CHAP</acronym> se ne razlikuje puno. Možete vidjeti &Linux; Vodič "
"Mrežnih Administratora za <filename>chap-secrets</filename> format datoteke, "
"a <application>pppd</application> korištenih argumenata, a ostatak bi trebao "
"biti jednostavan."
